#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128931 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "a6d910ae-c6db-51d2-93ba-f6c823c0a8c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-6179" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z= x^2 + xy$ at the point $(1,2, 3).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = (x-x_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0) + (y-y_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =2x+y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y) = (1,2)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2) & =2(1)+2=4 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-3 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) \\\\ z-3 & =4(x-1)+1(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =4x+y-6 \\\\ -4x-y+z+3 & =0 \\\\ 4x+y-z-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128932 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points at Which Tangent Planes Have Particular Properties"}] :question/id #uuid "4eb4806c-3d5b-5ed2-87a1-d1ed50c267e5" :question/math-academy-id "e-6182" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z={y^2}+ {xy}$  is the tangent plane horizontal?" :question/worked-solution "The tangent plane to a surface is horizontal if and only if the normal vector to the tangent plane is vertical. So, let's first find the general expression of a normal vector to the surface.\n\nRemember that the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = (x-x_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0) + (y-y_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\left\\langle \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0), \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0), -1 \\right\\rangle$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+xy) \\\\  & =2y+x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n\\left\\langle y, \\: 2y+x, \\: -1 \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe want to find where this normal vector is vertical. This means that the $x$- and $y$-components of the vector must be $0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064554/assets/a20e553b10de1d00abd5beead7766a1859073f07b1f5bfb734b51e8433fbeee0.png) \n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2(0) +x = 0 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x = 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=0$ and $y=0$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz = 0^2+(0)(0)= 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point where the tangent plane is horizontal is $(0,0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128934 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/id #uuid "ed1a3960-c2c4-57e7-8fd1-daf5d98bf052" :question/math-academy-id "e-6185" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=x^2+y^2+z^2-2xyz$ at the point $(1,-1,1,5).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $(x_0, y_0, z_0,w_0)$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw - w_0 = (x-x_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x_0,y_0,z_0) + (y-y_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x_0,y_0,z_0) + (z-z_0)\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}(x_0,y_0,z_0).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2xyz)=2x-2yz \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2xyz)=2y-2xz \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2xyz)=2z-2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z) = (1,-1,1)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1) & =2(1)-2(-1)(1)=4 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1) & =2(-1)-2(1)(1)=-4 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1) & =2(1)-2(1)(-1)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-5 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,-1,1)+(y+1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,-1,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,-1,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting and simplifying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-5 & =4(x-1)-4(y+1)+4(z-1) \\\\ w-5 & =4x-4y+4z-12 \\\\ -4x+4y-4z+w+7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-4y+4z-w-7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ea45773-5dc2-5c1f-83da-5187bc00921b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+y-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348470} {:answer/id #uuid "dcabd287-07c2-5681-9191-631ef448ebba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+3y-z-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348471} {:answer/id #uuid "773da438-c442-583c-8e9e-11595c71e411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-z+1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348472} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7476dc-b428-58b3-bce8-d8406cb9d550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y+z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348473} {:answer/id #uuid "f526dc2b-16d1-5572-9dd7-a1e9462a9592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+y-1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c7476dc-b428-58b3-bce8-d8406cb9d550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y+z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348473} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae8a321f-2980-59b1-98af-c12c53080ebc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90e1c765-c960-5941-8a93-9abc5a28c17f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129439" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z={x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+3$ at the point $(0,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+3) \\\\  & =2x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+3) \\\\  & =-4y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(0,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,1) & =2(0)=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,1) & =-4(1)=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & =(x-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,1)+(y-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,1) \\\\ z-1 & =0x-4(y-1) \\\\ z-1 & =-4y+4 \\\\ 4y+z-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f27abf79-95a6-5819-820e-eac04f27816f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y+z-4w+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348477} {:answer/id #uuid "9d3c5d31-3f05-5f24-a6b3-8cd180593d13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+2y-3z-12w+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348478} {:answer/id #uuid "129e93ca-0fd3-5df4-8037-7e48b9aeb60c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-z-8w+18=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348479} {:answer/id #uuid "acb65bae-e084-5330-83cc-4c90c091c5b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-y-2z-4w+22=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348480} {:answer/id #uuid "4616b928-99b4-5d03-be01-64e67dd4bcef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-y-2z+6w-1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d3c5d31-3f05-5f24-a6b3-8cd180593d13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+2y-3z-12w+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348478} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd5a3b42-aab1-5020-ab8c-460ccbc80003" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b72317b3-4faa-55e3-b429-89f16a23925d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129476" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z}$ at the point $(1,9,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z})=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,9,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,9,4) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,9,4) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{9}}=\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,9,4) & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-2 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,9,4)+(y-9)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,9,4)+(z-4)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,9,4) \\\\ w-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)+\\frac{1}{6}(y-9)-\\frac{1}{4}(z-4) \\\\ w-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{1}{4}z-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{1}{4}z-w+1 & =0 \\\\ 12(\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{1}{4}z-w+1) & =12\\cdot 0 \\\\ 6x+2y-3z-12w+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "947b1093-b6fd-5717-901a-d6a3443b5d34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+3y-2z+w-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348484} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f86b24-1eac-5dd1-a758-9a8d7491ccfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+y-z-w+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348485} {:answer/id #uuid "5ebdad9c-f0c8-57ad-a60b-243ef3cad494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-y-8z+4w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348486} {:answer/id #uuid "9f80c6a3-260c-50a1-b1d9-789d877e8141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+2y+z+w-8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348487} {:answer/id #uuid "2f5d850e-fcd8-5485-9d62-8577bc00460a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-y-z+2w+3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ebdad9c-f0c8-57ad-a60b-243ef3cad494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-y-8z+4w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348486} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f87321d-9888-5a51-916c-d81eba27d566" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348483}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2c46c90-d6c0-5141-8fe1-65f1ffc12e15" :question/math-academy-id "q-129483" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=z\\sqrt{y}-x$ at the point $(-1,4,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z\\sqrt{y}-x)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z\\sqrt{y}-x)=\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z\\sqrt{y}-x)=\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(-1,4,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(-1,4,1) & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(-1,4,1) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(-1,4,1) & =\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-3 & =(x-(-1))\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(-1,4,1)+(y-4)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(-1,4,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(-1,4,1) \\\\ w-3 & =-(x+1)+\\frac{1}{4}(y-4)+2(z-1) \\\\ w-3 & =-x+\\frac{1}{4}y+2z-4 \\\\ x-\\frac{1}{4}y-2z+w+1 & =0 \\\\ 4x-y-8z+4w+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46450c09-aa9b-59c9-bb0f-f56f8a0fd369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x-2y-2z-w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348491} {:answer/id #uuid "52d2c6f0-29be-59bb-9d03-d154b1aa21ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y+4z+w+\\pi -2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348492} {:answer/id #uuid "a5cce981-3237-5026-a755-8d4e90b7e941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y-w+\\pi +3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348493} {:answer/id #uuid "6915394d-f1b8-5e86-b91b-7b488626cf30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+w+\\pi +1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348494} {:answer/id #uuid "100e539b-0f50-5b03-8772-cf78a4cb236d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+\\pi z+w=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46450c09-aa9b-59c9-bb0f-f56f8a0fd369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x-2y-2z-w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348491} :answer-field/id #uuid "e452b7bf-c674-5669-9549-f8c32ea15fc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43f4cd3b-dc43-5995-818b-cf75242a740a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129485" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz)$ at the point $(-1,1,1,-\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz))=4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz))=\\frac{4xz}{1+{y}^{2}{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(yz))=\\frac{4xy}{1+{y}^{2}{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(-1,1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(-1,1,1) & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1\\cdot 1)=\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(-1,1,1) & =\\frac{4(-1)(1)}{1+({1}^{2})({1}^{2})}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(-1,1,1) & =\\frac{4(-1)(1)}{1+({1}^{2})({1}^{2})}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-(-\\pi ) & =(x-(-1))\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(-1,1,1)+(y-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(-1,1,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(-1,1,1) \\\\ w+\\pi  & =\\pi (x+1)-2(y-1)-2(z-1) \\\\ w+\\pi  & =\\pi x-2y-2z+4+\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x-2y-2z-w+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points at Which Tangent Planes Have Particular Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d48c872-f09d-5889-9d9c-4997c91d3b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(1,1,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348498} {:answer/id #uuid "75b94a8c-524e-542f-bfc9-f7980a899706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,1,-2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348499} {:answer/id #uuid "5f4d6c95-4334-50fd-8e86-5afe803ea81d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,1,2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348500} {:answer/id #uuid "527ed532-2522-58d7-a138-f2d0de66bda0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348501} {:answer/id #uuid "22cc270c-3435-50df-8d40-fb48bbc4745a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,1,-2)$ and $(1,1,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "527ed532-2522-58d7-a138-f2d0de66bda0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348501} :answer-field/id #uuid "db2b26e2-4cc8-5797-9c2d-7f87cc090d28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d46b44a-f954-58c4-a226-1cd197027a06" :question/math-academy-id "q-129554" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z={x}^{3}+xy$ is the tangent plane horizontal?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}+xy)=3{x}^{2}+y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}+xy)=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨3{x}^{2}+y,\\,x,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNote that the tangent plane is horizontal if and only if the normal vector is vertical. This means that the $x$- and $y$-components of the vector must be $0:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+y=0 \\\\ x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the second equation we get $x=0.$ Substituting $x=0$ into first equation, we obtain $y=0.$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=0$ and $y=0$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz={0}^{3}+0(0)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point where the tangent plane is horizontal is $(0,0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8507d7e-07a3-5d8f-93ce-433486374489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x + 4y - z - 5 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127089} {:answer/id #uuid "dffdace6-2778-5d3d-a4cf-b5557a59f7e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x + 4y - z - 5 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127090} {:answer/id #uuid "10481073-7643-573d-b44e-7eadc4ee4f38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8x + 3y - z - 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127091} {:answer/id #uuid "11de7225-ee75-5bfc-9dda-68fef1ce7ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x + 4y - z - 5 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127092} {:answer/id #uuid "39fbe8b3-8ab5-55d2-9ac4-40a876722f4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x + 6y - z - 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8507d7e-07a3-5d8f-93ce-433486374489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x + 4y - z - 5 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127089} :answer-field/id #uuid "fca92eb9-afdc-5ad0-81ea-ce97504ba91d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab92392f-12a1-569b-997c-793bd45fc373" :question/math-academy-id "q-37595" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z={y}^{2}{e}^{2x}-1$ at the point $(0,2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}{e}^{2x}-1) \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}{e}^{2x}-1) \\\\  & =2y{e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,2) & =2(2)^{2}{e}^{2(0)}=8 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,2) & =2(2){e}^{2(0)}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-3 & =(x-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(0,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(0,2) \\\\ z-3 & =8(x-0)+4(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =8x+4y-8 \\\\ -8x-4y+z+5 & =0 \\\\ 8x+4y-z-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89d3e2ce-c323-5a87-9059-fa6e0b841701" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+4y-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348505} {:answer/id #uuid "6708bb11-6bed-52ba-b65a-8bf0e360780b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348506} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac77240-481e-539a-9f99-69359ec52e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+4y-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348507} {:answer/id #uuid "122dd92e-06c0-5327-9951-998eb44820ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y+4x-z+1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348508} {:answer/id #uuid "6697061a-30ae-56c5-a6d4-d4059c61eb3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y+4x-z+1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6708bb11-6bed-52ba-b65a-8bf0e360780b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348506} :answer-field/id #uuid "b46b0017-5c4c-523b-8c58-6f718b5f2edd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d17cf951-6ee2-5ad5-bc9f-bb9fae13cb30" :question/math-academy-id "q-37715" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{2}y)-{y}^{3}$ at the point $(2,0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{2}y)-{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}+1}\\cdot 2xy \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{2}y)-{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}+1}\\cdot {x}^{2}-3{y}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}+1}-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(2,0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,0) & =\\frac{2(2)(0)}{(2)^{4}(0)^{2}+1}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,0) & =\\frac{(2)^{2}}{(2)^{4}(0)^{2}+1}-3(0)^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-0 & =(x-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,0)+(y-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,0) \\\\ z & =0(x-0)+4(y-0) \\\\ z & =4y \\\\ 4y-z & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points at Which Tangent Planes Have Particular Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e524bd42-9c44-5bee-bb30-9e6c8801f7fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pi ,2,-2\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348512} {:answer/id #uuid "aa56ae7d-ad7c-508d-80bf-9ff480fb559f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\pi ,\\pi ,12\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348513} {:answer/id #uuid "c7006f14-3fd7-567a-a4af-733f1781a533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\pi ,-\\pi ,2\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348514} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e86711-1a46-5c53-bdd9-60c077097c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,6,8\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348515} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c99ec5-76b1-55a1-a949-d7f6a32a4f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\pi ,\\pi ,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e524bd42-9c44-5bee-bb30-9e6c8801f7fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pi ,2,-2\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348512} :answer-field/id #uuid "b97a533a-504c-5fad-9d62-b4a4e0d4a9a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "89fc1719-eff0-5a8a-ab75-2f9cb836c01b" :question/math-academy-id "q-37986" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-xy$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector  $v\\,=\\,⟨8,2\\pi ,2⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-xy) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-xy) \\\\  & =-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-y,\\,-x,\\,-1⟩\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨8,2\\pi ,2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-y,\\,-x,\\,-1⟩=⟨8,2\\pi ,2⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2c\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-cy=8 \\\\ -xc=2\\pi  \\\\ -c=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=-2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-x(-2)=2\\pi \\,⟹\\,x=\\pi .\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=-2$ and $x=\\pi $ into the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n2(-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -(-2)y=8\\,⟹\\,y=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=\\pi $ and $y=2$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-xy \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -(\\pi )(2) \\\\  & =-2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector  $v$ at $(\\pi ,2,-2\\pi ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points at Which Tangent Planes Have Particular Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fffecbfa-cea8-5328-8cc6-180c9e753b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348519} {:answer/id #uuid "857b4c4f-668e-5f69-9a9b-5b4dd8cb8f8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348520} {:answer/id #uuid "1610b567-2ca3-55b2-ba8c-e2fcbb524d1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,0,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348521} {:answer/id #uuid "240106e2-b28f-579d-9d76-092314153448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,1,-6)$, $(1,0,-6)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348522} {:answer/id #uuid "d2557a60-daa4-5963-b007-1d8ef1e87236" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-6)$, $(1,0,-6)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fffecbfa-cea8-5328-8cc6-180c9e753b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348519} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec6e7e90-5dd0-5f74-9ed1-9bd40e6f72bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "780b4002-68c1-540d-b811-b3bb4089819e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37990" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z=4{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{3}-6$  is the tangent plane \nhorizontal?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{3}-6) \\\\  & =8xy+{y}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{3}-6) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨8xy+{y}^{3},\\,4{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2},\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNote that the tangent plane is horizontal if and only if the normal vector is vertical. This means that the $x$- and $y$-components of the vector must be $0:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}8xy+{y}^{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y=0$ or ${y}^{2}+8x=0.$ So, we have two cases.\n\n- If $y=0$, substituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+3x(0)^{2}=0\\,⟹\\,x=0.\n$$\n\n- If ${y}^{2}=-8x$, substituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+3x(-8x)^{2}=0\\,⟹\\,x=0.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0$ back into ${y}^{2}=-8x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-8(0)\\,⟹\\,y=0.\n$$\n\nSo, in both cases, we have $x=0$ and $y=0.$ Finally, substituting these values into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz=4(0)^{2}(0)+(0)(0)^{3}-6=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point where the tangent plane is horizontal is $(0,0,-6).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbbd1a17-9cc1-5883-961f-b5c7ee97da61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-5y-2z-8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348526} {:answer/id #uuid "d80d10d5-393c-59c8-b8ca-4f2cd2ae75a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+5y-2z-8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348527} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc13cff-4e1e-5803-bd25-ad3dc8e4f327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+5y-2z+14=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348528} {:answer/id #uuid "f0086af7-f409-5c69-b198-47da7a03f97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+5y-z-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348529} {:answer/id #uuid "5310ee80-5b69-5ced-9c15-afba5ae8792b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-5y+2z-36=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d80d10d5-393c-59c8-b8ca-4f2cd2ae75a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+5y-2z-8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348527} :answer-field/id #uuid "da365fbb-eb87-5d32-b561-280b1e4ac536" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "319f4b72-4b6d-5a27-96a0-4ff226793195" :question/math-academy-id "q-73841" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=\\sqrt{xy}+xy$ at the point $(2,2,6).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{xy}+xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{xy}}+y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{2\\sqrt{x}}+y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xy}+xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{xy}}+x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2\\sqrt{y}}+x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(2,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+2=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+2=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-6 & =(x-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2) \\\\ z-6 & =\\frac{5}{2}(x-2)+\\frac{5}{2}(y-2) \\\\ z-6 & =\\frac{5x}{2}+\\frac{5y}{2}-10 \\\\ 2z-12 & =5x+5y-20 \\\\ -5x-5y+2z+8 & =0 \\\\ 5x+5y-2z-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4de868c0-80b7-5cbb-9dc2-ba04493471fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cab1c79-0aaf-5084-a092-77719ddaf838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y-z+1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348533} {:answer/id #uuid "897add59-cbb3-5f10-ba70-b319f5328878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y-z-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348534} {:answer/id #uuid "0f87b44e-71a2-58e7-932e-8b7b6fca4a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y+z-1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348535} {:answer/id #uuid "22ef6674-c9a0-5413-a555-b2f647142a9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y-z-1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348536} {:answer/id #uuid "c547799a-7ca2-53e5-8029-8bfa6dc9d4bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22ef6674-c9a0-5413-a555-b2f647142a9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y-z-1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348536} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0cd58ce-5fa6-5f11-b56b-f518d331b986" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "803bd311-37cf-5c07-b46d-292be85851d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73842" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1$ at the point $(1,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1) & =\\frac{1}{1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{1}{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1)+(y-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1) \\\\ z-1 & =1\\cdot (x-1)+1\\cdot (y-1) \\\\ z-1 & =x+y-2 \\\\ -x-y+z+1 & =0 \\\\ x+y-z-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ec1d482-1886-57f2-b8d5-91c9fb1d021a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x+\\pi y+z-w+3\\pi =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348540} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b46d28-1748-5833-b147-e17dcd997ab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x+\\pi y+z+w-3\\pi =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348541} {:answer/id #uuid "18b195d3-ad1b-58a8-8243-b1ab1da607a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x-\\pi y+z+w-\\pi =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348542} {:answer/id #uuid "20dcf995-6d15-551d-9e56-de806e79e85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x-\\pi y-z+w+\\pi =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348543} {:answer/id #uuid "92299bda-07bb-5d8e-a66a-59b239344cd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x+\\pi y-z+w-\\pi =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8b46d28-1748-5833-b147-e17dcd997ab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi x+\\pi y+z+w-3\\pi =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348541} :answer-field/id #uuid "c845015d-222f-5de0-ab30-d9cc4b885fab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ffcf1e6-dd79-52ee-b822-590a68f4e687" :question/math-academy-id "q-73851" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)$ at the point $(1,1,\\pi ,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz))=yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz))=xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz))=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,1,\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1,\\pi ) & =(1)(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 1\\cdot \\pi )=-\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1,\\pi ) & =(1)(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 1\\cdot \\pi )=-\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,1,\\pi ) & =(1)(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 1\\cdot \\pi )=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-0 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,1,\\pi )+(y-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,1,\\pi )+(z-\\pi )\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,1,\\pi ) \\\\ w & =-\\pi (x-1)-\\pi (y-1)-(z-\\pi ) \\\\ w & =-\\pi x+\\pi -\\pi y+\\pi -z+\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x+\\pi y+z+w-3\\pi  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc56f7a5-65a7-53a9-9eb6-ae7b91a1bdd0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Hyperplane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "493bce95-f6c0-5662-a039-f3be1be1e7da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+z+w-12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348547} {:answer/id #uuid "0c8ab8c0-c3b0-59a8-a08d-a31aec9c91dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y-z-w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348548} {:answer/id #uuid "47ce431d-c34f-5981-a94d-8a0bcfac8c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y-z+w-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348549} {:answer/id #uuid "ef944206-a493-552e-a573-dcf2ae35b428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y+z-w=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348550} {:answer/id #uuid "5f491606-44a6-52ce-a592-af989f4e983b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+z-w=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f491606-44a6-52ce-a592-af989f4e983b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+z-w=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348551} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1eb8af4-73ab-5824-9384-e869ab499363" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96fd3eb5-4bb3-509e-9a64-1f3114cc6b99" :question/math-academy-id "q-73852" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+\\sqrt{zx}$ at the point $(2,2,2,6).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+\\sqrt{zx})=\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{z}}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+\\sqrt{zx})=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{z}}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+\\sqrt{zx})=\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{2\\sqrt{z}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2\\sqrt{z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(2,2,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2,2) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2,2) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,2,2) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-6 & =(x-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2,2)+(z-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,2,2) \\\\ w-6 & =(x-2)+(y-2)+(z-2) \\\\ w-6 & =x+y+z-6 \\\\ -x-y-z+w & =0 \\\\ x+y+z-w & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points at Which Tangent Planes Have Particular Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2824d78-468c-5cf4-920f-28a63ab18cfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-3,0)$ and $(-1,3,28)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348554} {:answer/id #uuid "32e6a3f4-ba6a-5184-b250-a72c1d19fe57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,3,28)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348555} {:answer/id #uuid "4780c6cf-0192-5297-ae6c-24e9a48f9aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-3,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348556} {:answer/id #uuid "05e85d9b-270e-5f9c-b1df-9952bdf6728d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,3,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348557} {:answer/id #uuid "bccc0cdf-bfdf-537a-b8f0-ed8cc8b7d97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-3,0)$ and $(3,1,20)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4780c6cf-0192-5297-ae6c-24e9a48f9aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(1,-3,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348556} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b4a1090-cf8b-5d65-b018-1fecca039b03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a1a92dc-c845-5e19-ad17-e7014a5b5299" :question/math-academy-id "q-73857" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z={x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}+6y+10$ is the tangent plane horizontal?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}+6y+10) \\\\  & =2x-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}+6y+10) \\\\  & =2y+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨2x-2,\\,2y+6,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNote that the tangent plane is horizontal if and only if the normal vector is vertical. This means that the $x$- and $y$-components of the vector must be $0:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2x-2=0 \\\\ 2y+6=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=1$ while the second equation gives $y=-3.$ \n\nFinally, substituting $x=1$ and $y=-3$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\nz={1}^{2}-2(1)+(-3)^{2}+6(-3)+10=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point where the tangent plane is horizontal is $(1,-3,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cc25edf-9d32-5b47-ae4f-e370d2d0d024" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points at Which Tangent Planes Have Particular Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6ada0f0-b511-5de7-b2eb-d461dbfce816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,0,-1)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348561} {:answer/id #uuid "19fbb863-1726-5fd5-8a92-07e35694a87b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-1,0,-1)$ and $(1,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348562} {:answer/id #uuid "f8dc1eac-4f8c-5ebf-8ff5-fa252384f84e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,0,2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348563} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d22eac-96b2-54b7-b020-04f870f32d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,0,-2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348564} {:answer/id #uuid "c4249a52-391c-5539-9ed4-12286dce157a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,0,-2)$ and $(2,0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6d22eac-96b2-54b7-b020-04f870f32d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,0,-2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348564} :answer-field/id #uuid "345c08cd-5cae-5fe9-a726-2978ed622e4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4dda47ef-07a9-5b66-b0c0-061f88baf1dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-73869" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z=x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector  $v\\,=\\,⟨-2,4,2⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨{e}^{y},\\,x{e}^{y}+2y,\\,-1⟩\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨-2,4,2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨{e}^{y},\\,x{e}^{y}+2y,\\,-1⟩=⟨-2,4,2⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}c{e}^{y}=-2 \\\\ cx{e}^{y}+2cy=4 \\\\ -c=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=-2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-2{e}^{y}=-2\\,⟹\\,y=0.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=-2$ and $y=0$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n-2x{e}^{0}+2(-2)(0)=4\\,⟹\\,x=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=-2$ and $y=0$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2} \\\\  & =(-2){e}^{0}+{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(-2,0,-2).$"}]}
